From 210fb3629a7f045ea1afb051fc2846c6e03581b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Solhex <solhex@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:46:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] ytm_bridge: converge on the right cover after a track
 change

A browser publishes the new track before it has the new artwork: for a moment
the media session still returns the previous track's thumbnail. Reading the
cover once per track therefore pinned the old album art on the device for the
whole song (seen on Windows, where 'art 269 bytes' was missing from the log for
every other track).

Read the thumbnail again for the first few seconds of a track, and keep asking
on a slower timer if it never turns up at all. The bytes are still only turned
into a frame when they differ from the last one sent.
