pythonw.exe (what the logon shortcut runs) has no console, so spawning the
console-subsystem yt-dlp made Windows allocate one: a Windows Terminal window
titled '...\yt-dlp.exe' appeared for the length lookup on each new track.

Pass CREATE_NO_WINDOW (plus SW_HIDE) for that call, and for the installer's
PowerShell calls. Measured from pythonw: without it a CASCADIA_HOSTING_WINDOW_CLASS
window appears and is gone when the child exits; with it, none — while the lookup
still returns a duration.
